s  i will be going away in about eight days  to virginia  but i would be lying to you if i said  everything was business as usual because  it's not  i had to do this extensive packing list  got the big bottle hand sanitizer though  had to get the lysol spray and had to  get those clorox wipes  i'm torn i'm trying to find ways that i  can kind of feel  positive about how things are gonna go  but i find it hard to  forget about all the things that we are  losing  [Music]  i found out about two days before i was  supposed to leave for new york  to start quarantining at barnard in  colombia  made the decision to go remote this  semester i feel like  my life has been flipped upside down  about like five different times in the  past week  i am definitely not excited to take a  coronavirus test rate the second i get  to school  which is gonna definitely be an  unpleasant experience from what i've  heard  i got my schedule and i realized all of  my classes were online  so then i was like wow i'm not gonna get  my freshman year experience either  i had wanted to show you all kind of  where  my internship took place but also where  my classes will this fall semester it is  my room in fact i never want to get the  virus  so at least being at home lowers that  risk but  it is frustrating why am i always the  one making decisions  my emotions about the future are very  mixed  i just got to new york the other day and  i'm moving  into an apartment with two other barnard  girls i'm really excited to finally be  independent  to be living on my own i reached out to  um  many kids on like facebook and instagram  and i met so many great people through  there that are  also going to slow and i've been getting  to know them  it's been really great it's just times  like these you just gotta appreciate  everything you have  and so never take anything in your life  for granted because you never know when  it could be stripped away from you let's  go  class of 2020 we're definitely the  strongest class  no matter what challenges come our way  we're always gonna face them head-on  everyone seems to be going out of their  way to meet others  um i think that's ultimately the best  thing that we can do is just trying to  make the best of our situations  i'm way more hopeful about how these  next few months are going to turn out  than i was even two weeks ago  so yeah i think that's a perfect way to  end it  [Music]  wow you really feel for these kids you  really do think of all the stuff  i like why georgia what you said we've  had a lot of stuff thrown at us yeah i  also like wyatt's blue  wig i like why george but just think  remember how excited we were to go to  college when you went you're looking  forward to this well for senior year of  high school and freshman year of college  doubly gypped and deprived getting  sheets and tells they got clorox  special shout out to eliana mentz who  was the one that put that together those  are very hard to do  eliana love your music choices we'll be  right back stay with us  we'll be right back  you're watching cbs this morning
 

